### **FAILURE**

- Vacuum-assisted birth has failed if:
 - the fetal head does not advance with each pull;
 - there is no descent of the baby's head after three pulls with no descent;
 - the cup slips off the head twice at the proper direction of pull with maximum negative pressure.
- Every application should be considered as a test of the obstetric vacuum. Do not persist if there is no descent after three pulls.

